<!--
  The two numbers on the enclosure are release-owner inputs, not documentation:

    length             byte size of artifacts/Submit-<version>-macOS.zip
    sparkle:edSignature base64 Ed25519 signature over the exact bytes
                       "<version>\n<download URL>" (see
                       UpdateEngine.signaturePayload) using the offline release
                       key whose public half is UpdateEngine.updatePublicKeyBase64.

  tools/update_appcast.sh writes both, given the version, the built zip, and the
  path to the release update private key. It refuses a key that does not verify
  against the shipped public key, so a mistake here fails loudly.

  UpdateEngine refuses an enclosure with no signature while requireSignature is
  true, so an unsigned feed shows up as "no update offered" rather than as a
  download of something unverified. That is the intended failure: sign the feed
  before it goes live.
-->
